Z||000011||Mach10||10-16-2001||06:15 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><BR>It's not just new hookups. They've shut down all non-critical operations for the duration of the bankruptcy proceedings. Anything database related cannot be touched. So if you go down for database reasons (corrupt account key, loss of provisioning etc), you pretty much stay down. <BR>@home isn't local, it's all across North America (Not sure about Mexico, though). They provide the backbone and infrastructure, and lease it out to MSOs, (like Cox, AT&T, Shaw, Media1, Comcast etc) who provide the service. There's a lot of people getting screwed, and a lot of helpless techs (me) getting yelled at.||||reg||13
